rtist":"Lycia","year":1993,"weight":7,"yt":"K6Y7lQjwNOc","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":59251635065665,"name":"Sputnikmusic Best Albums 1993","rank":81,"scaruffi":8.0},{"id":13018320481353,"name":"Scaruffi 1990s","rank":89,"scaruffi":8.0}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":137033996990045,"type":"album","name":"The Burning Circle And Then Dust","artist":"Lycia","year":1995,"weight":6,"yt":"DrKuoPqu9n8","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":13018320481353,"name":"Scaruffi 1990s","rank":90,"scaruffi":8.0}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":127013640863346,"type":"album","name":"The Scavenger Bride","artist":"Black Tape For A Blue Girl","year":2002,"weight":6,"yt":"w79PjCiFVMo","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":76687108203,"name":"Scaruffi 2000s","rank":233,"scaruffi":7.0}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":59063887462151,"type":"album","name":"The Land Of Harm And Appletrees","artist":"Aurora","year":1993,"weight":6,"yt":"gQp1zG_NlL0","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":13018320481353,"name":"Scaruffi 1990s","rank":161,"scaruffi":7.5}],"n_lists":1}}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Emergence (1979)","body":"Dark Wave was potentially emerging in 1979, alongside New Wave and other nascent styles that would eventually contribute to gothic and sinister music. This period, from 1977 to 1981, was highly dynamic in music history. \"estaban naciendo la vez posible en el dar wave y muchas partes de lo que sería luego la música agótica y siniestra.\"","year":1979,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Especial JOY DIVISION: 2. Unknown Pleasures","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I9nK6TmzqGs"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Defining Sound of \"Música Máquina\" at Espiral","body":"Dark Wave was a significant genre contributing to the \"música máquina\" sound that characterized Espiral, known as \"the toughest club in the east\" for its hard-hitting sound. This genre, along with EBM and industrial music, shaped Espiral's intense musical identity. \"Su sonido era uno de los más duros de la ruta, e incluía generos como el FM, el Dark Waze, or Noid Diswell, los cuales irían definiendo el sonido de la música máquina.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Central Sonora","episode":"Cuando Valencia fue la capital mundial del Clubbing","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ckJgog8P_og"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Description","body":"Dark wave is highlighted as a key characteristic of The Soft Moon's album *Original*, emphasizing its super industrial sound. \"es como super, super industrial, rollo dark wave.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Lanzamientos Febrero  2018","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pO_KgN9SRK4"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Emergence in Early 1980s","body":"In the early 1980s, specific sub-genres began to emerge from the broader New Wave movement. Dark Wave was one such genre, originating from bands like Siouxsie and the Banshees and The Cure, further diversifying the alternative music landscape. \"teníamos el Dark Wave, que es el que vendría de Xi Xi and the Bansis o el que vendría de Kyur.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Que es el New Wave","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jxaTsoSRXZE"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"First Indie Generation Label","body":"Dark Wave is one of the names used to describe the first significant generation of indie music, which emerged between 1978 and 1982 and included bands like Joy Division, R.E.M., The Cure, and The Smiths. \"Dark Waves, todos estos nombres que se deponen a esa generación que salía joydivision.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"La generación perdida del Indie: SHOEGAZE","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kbiXssvv3aE"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Proposed Label for Joy Division","body":"\"Dark Wave\" was suggested as a potential descriptor for Joy Division's unique post-punk sound, which was characterized by brooding lyrics and low-voiced singers, as attempts were made to categorize their uncategorizable style. \"Is this a dark wave? Okay, that might work.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Post-Punk Explosion Part 7: All the rest","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LgJ7ww2AgF4"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Subgenre of Post-Punk","body":"Dark Wave is identified as one of the styles that falls under the post-punk umbrella. \"Goth, dark wave, dream pop, the jangly guitars, bands like R.E.M., the spiky stuff of groups like Wire and Shoegay's were, and in some cases still are, artists in those buckets that we can consider to be post-punk.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"What Exactly is Post-Rock? Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pLf3kUONewg"}]}]}